<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px"><h2 id="faq-h" style="font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,36px);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em">Automated Communications questions</h2><a href="/faq?topic=com" style="font-weight:600;font-size:16px">See all questions →</a></div>
<div style="min-width:0;border-bottom:1px solid #DED5C6">
<details open="" style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x3" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Will it message people without our approval?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">No. Messages run only through workflows your team approves, and sensitive or consequential messages wait for a person.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x4" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Can a person check a message before it goes out?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Yes. Any step in a workflow can be set to wait for approval.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x5" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">What kinds of messages can it send?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Confirmations, follow-ups, reminders and notifications. Each one can go by text, email, WhatsApp or phone call, whichever suits your customers.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x6" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Who's responsible for consent?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">You are, for your own contacts. We set workflows up so messages go only to people you're permitted to contact.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x7" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">How is Automated Communications priced?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Pricing is custom, based on your use case and complexity. It's month-to-month with no setup fee for the standard service, and usage, such as text messages, WhatsApp messages and call minutes, is billed at actual provider cost with no markup.</p></details>
</div>
